id: decisions/021-status-dimensionality
title: "Standing is several keys, each closed, lifecycle required"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'status-dimensionality'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: status-dimensionality
axis_gloss: "whether a record's standing is reported as several orthogonal axes, or collapsed into one value"
poles:
  a: multi-axis-status
  b: single-scalar-status
split: leaning
draft_status: full
leverage: 13.4
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(16) x split_weight(0.7) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  Is a record's standing one lifecycle word, or several independent axes — and
  if several, must each be its own top-level key with its own closed list, or is
  the eight-dimension statuses.v1 object the shape every record must carry?

why_it_matters: >
  A bot that asks 'what is active?' or 'what is proved?' cannot get an answer
  from the tree today, because one status: word carried four meanings across 176
  files, the eight-dimension contract has zero users, and the six-member labels
  list in core/proof-and-boundary.yawn mixes modal, motivational and epistemic
  terms in a single line. Once answered, every record and bot below Dave reads
  standing from a fixed set of keys, so a child Yawn's ratified, observed and
  moving can never be confused for one another.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    12 judgments sit at multi-axis-status (8 authored) and 4 at
    single-scalar-status (0 authored). The repository asserts both directions on
    this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave wants authority_status or ratification_status as the canonical
    key name (both are in use); and whether presentation_status and
    axis_resolution_status belong on records at all or only on Views and receipts.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: Every canonical record carries all eight status dimensions as separate
      top-level snake_case keys — status (lifecycle), epistemic_status,
      authority_status, loop_status, modal_role, motivational_role,
      axis_resolution_status, presentation_status — each drawn from statuses.v1's
      enum. The labels list in core/proof-and-boundary.yawn is split into the three
      dimensions it mixes (known, proved, unproven are epistemic; imagined is modal;
      desired is motivational).
    cost: "176 records gain up to seven keys; statuses.v1's epistemicStatus enum (eight values) must first be reconciled with the seven-value canonical the test enforces (GROUND_TRUTH fact 1); most records have no honest value for presentation_status or axis_resolution_status."
    risk: "Seven mandatory keys get filled with neutral or unknown to satisfy a test, which is the same uncomputable noise as free text, now typed."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend tests/status-vocabulary.test.mjs to require all eight keys on records outside a shrink-only ledger and validate each against statuses.v1 after its epistemicStatus enum is aligned to the seven canonical values; a test that core/proof-and-boundary.yawn labels no longer mixes dimensions."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0304"
      - "J0452"
      - "J0519"
      - "J0671"
      - "J0122"
      - "J0190"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: status: is the only standing field a record carries. Other dimensions
      are expressed in prose or dropped; statuses.v1.schema.json is archived;
      status_rule in schemas/node.yawn and separate_status_dimensions in
      core/proof-and-boundary.yawn are struck.
    cost: "Strikes three authored records (schemas/node.yawn status_rule, interface/meaning.yawn status_dimensions, question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn separate_metrics); the routing contract's three confidences and the objective-holon ratification flow lose their vocabulary."
    risk: "epistemic_status: proposed (J0768) becomes normal again — authority words drift back into the epistemic field because there is nowhere else to put them."
    reversibility: false
    proof_needed: "The existing tests/status-vocabulary.test.mjs as-is; archive schemas/statuses.v1.schema.json; delete the epistemic_status test."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0129"
      - "J0263"
      - "J0327"
      - "J0768"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: Standing is multi-axis, each dimension its own top-level key with its
      own closed vocabulary, and only lifecycle (status:) is required on every
      record. The other seven are optional; when present they are validated against
      statuses.v1, whose `required` is relaxed to lifecycleStatus alone and whose
      epistemicStatus enum is aligned to the seven canonical values. Consumers must
      not infer one dimension from another. The labels list in
      core/proof-and-boundary.yawn is rewritten as three short lists under
      separate_status_dimensions.
    cost: "Edit statuses.v1.schema.json (required, epistemicStatus); extend one test with per-key enums for authority_status/ratification_status, loop_status, modal_role, motivational_role; rewrite one list in core/proof-and-boundary.yawn; migrate readme.yawn's two epistemic_status: proposed tags to authority_status: proposed."
    risk: "Optional keys stay absent almost everywhere, so multi-axis standing exists in the vocabulary but not in the corpus, and a bot still cannot ask 'what is ratified?' across records that never say."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend tests/status-vocabulary.test.mjs: wherever authority_status, ratification_status, loop_status, modal_role or motivational_role appears, its value is in statuses.v1's enum; statuses.v1 epistemicStatus equals the CANONICAL set in tests/epistemic-status-vocabulary.test.mjs; core/proof-and-boundary.yawn labels are a subset of the union of the dimension enums and each maps to exactly one dimension."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0304"
      - "J0452"
      - "J0519"
      - "J0122"
      - "J0768"
      - "J0263"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.8
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    The passing suite already implements C's spine and says so in its own error
    message: tests/status-vocabulary.test.mjs closes top-level status: to the five
    lifecycle values and tells the writer to put version in spec_version,
    authority in ratification_status, loop position in loop_status — separate
    keys, one scalar each. tests/epistemic-status-vocabulary.test.mjs closes the
    second key. Side A is authored (eight of twelve) and states independence as a
    rule three times (schemas/node.yawn, interface/meaning.yawn,
    orientation-nine); side B is entirely REVEALED and mostly drift, though J0768
    (proposed used as an epistemic value in the root orientation card) shows the
    confusion is real, not cosmetic. A's eight mandatory keys is what statuses.v1
    literally requires and what zero records satisfy — GROUND_TRUTH fact 2 — so A
    would be a rule the corpus has already voted against by never using it. What
    remains after C is the three-vocabulary split in fact 1, which C's proof
    reconciles. Not close on direction; the only judgment call is
    required-versus-optional for the seven non-lifecycle keys.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "schemas/statuses.v1.schema.json requires only lifecycleStatus and its epistemicStatus enum equals the seven-value canonical set; tests/epistemic-status-vocabulary.test.mjs asserts the equality."
    - "core/proof-and-boundary.yawn labels: is split into three lists under separate_status_dimensions and no list mixes dimensions."
    - "readme.yawn's orientation card carries no epistemic_status: proposed; authority words live under authority_status or ratification_status."
    - "A test in tests/ rejects an out-of-enum value in any of the eight dimension keys wherever it appears, and passes."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A record carries authority_status: proposed under epistemic_status, or a loop
    word under status:, and npm test stays green; or statuses.v1 keeps requiring
    all eight dimensions while no record satisfies it.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0122"
  - "J0190"
  - "J0304"
  - "J0452"
  - "J0519"
  - "J0671"
  - "J0129"
  - "J0263"
  - "J0327"
  - "J0768"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
